ins now?**  \n   - If I play I7 now, does it make 5 vertically? I7, I8, I9, I10, I11 — all X’s except I7 is empty now. Playing I7 makes 5 in a row vertically (I7–I11). That’s a win.  \n\nLet’s verify:  \nI7 is empty (board shows column I row 7 = dot).  \nI8=X, I9=X, I10=X, I11=X.  \nYes, I7 connects them to 5.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nI7 is not in the occupied list, so it’s legal. It creates a vertical 5-in-a-row for Black, winning the game immediately. No need to consider opponent blocks because it’s game over.\n\n**Answer:**  \n{"col": "I", "row": 7}'}
